      "html" : "<\/div><div style=\"margin-bottom=10pt\">&#160;<\/div><\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><div id=\"rid-0-0-0-181816\" class=\"rbox Normal-Level\"><AnnotationDrawer recordId=\"0-0-0-181816\"><\/AnnotationDrawer><div class=\"Small\"><div style=\"margin-left:18pt;text-indent:-18pt;\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tFor SI: 1 inch = 25.4 mm<\/div><\/div><\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><div id=\"rid-0-0-0-181817\" class=\"rbox Normal-Level\"><AnnotationDrawer recordId=\"0-0-0-181817\"><\/AnnotationDrawer><div class=\"Small\"><div style=\"margin-left:18pt;text-indent:-18pt;\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\ta.&#160;&#160;&#160;Nails shall be driven perpendicular to the lamination face, alternating between top and bottom edges.<\/div><\/div><\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><div id=\"rid-0-0-0-181818\" class=\"rbox Normal-Level\"><AnnotationDrawer recordId=\"0-0-0-181818\"><\/AnnotationDrawer><div class=\"Small\"><div style=\"margin-left:18pt;text-indent:-18pt;\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tb.&#160;&#160;&#160;Where nails penetrate through two laminations and into the third, they shall be staggered one-third of the spacing in adjacent laminations. Otherwise, nails shall be staggered one-half of the spacing in adjacent laminations.<\/div><\/div><\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><div id=\"rid-0-0-0-181819\" class=\"rbox Normal-Level\"><AnnotationDrawer recordId=\"0-0-0-181819\"><\/AnnotationDrawer><div class=\"Small\"><div style=\"margin-left:18pt;text-indent:-18pt;\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tc.&#160;&#160;&#160;Two side nails shall be installed at each end of butt-jointed pieces.<\/div><\/div><\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><div id=\"rid-0-0-0-181820\" class=\"rbox Normal-Level\"><AnnotationDrawer recordId=\"0-0-0-181820\"><\/AnnotationDrawer><div class=\"Small\"><div style=\"margin-left:18pt;text-indent:-18pt;\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\td.&#160;&#160;&#160;Where supports are 48 inches (1219 mm) on center or less, alternate laminations shall be toenailed to alternate supports; where supports are spaced more than 48 inches (1219 mm) on center, alternate laminations shall be toenailed to every support.<\/div><\/div><\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><\/div>",
      "id" : "4917-html-3",
      "kind" : "html",
      "plainText" : "For SI: 1 inch = 25.4 mm\n\n a. Nails shall be driven perpendicular to the lamination face, alternating between top and bottom edges.\n\n b. Where nails penetrate through two laminations and into the third, they shall be staggered one-third of the spacing in adjacent laminations. Otherwise, nails shall be staggered one-half of the spacing in adjacent laminations.\n\n c. Two side nails shall be installed at each end of butt-jointed pieces.\n\n d. Where supports are 48 inches (1219 mm) on center or less, alternate laminations shall be toenailed to alternate supports; where supports are spaced more than 48 inches (1219 mm) on center, alternate laminations shall be toenailed to every support."
